#: ../../src/udp.rst:96
msgid ""
"`nread`:  Number of bytes that have been received. 0 if there is no more "
"data to read. Note that 0 may also mean that an empty datagram was "
"received (in this case `addr` is not NULL). < 0 if a transmission error "
"was detected; if using :man:`recvmmsg(2)` no more chunks will be received"
" and the buffer can be freed safely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:101
msgid "`buf`: :c:type:`uv_buf_t` with the received data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:102
msgid ""
"`addr`: ``struct sockaddr*`` containing the address of the sender. Can be"
" NULL. Valid for the duration of the callback only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:104
msgid "`flags`: One or more or'ed UV_UDP_* constants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:106
msgid ""
"The callee is responsible for freeing the buffer, libuv does not reuse "
"it. The buffer may be a null buffer (where `buf->base` == NULL and "
"`buf->len` == 0) on error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:110
msgid ""
"When using :man:`recvmmsg(2)`, chunks will have the `UV_UDP_MMSG_CHUNK` "
"flag set, those must not be freed. If no errors occur, there will be a "
"final callback with `nread` set to 0, `addr` set to NULL and the buffer "
"pointing at the initially allocated data with the `UV_UDP_MMSG_CHUNK` "
"flag cleared and the `UV_UDP_MMSG_FREE` flag set. If a UDP socket error "
"occurs, `nread` will be < 0. In either scenario, the callee can now "
"safely free the provided buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:117
msgid "added the `UV_UDP_MMSG_FREE` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/udp.rst:120
msgid ""
"The receive callback will be called with `nread` == 0 and `addr` == NULL "
"when there is nothing to read, and with `nread` == 0 and `addr` != NULL "
"when an empty UDP packet is received."
msgstr ""

